# EXTRA EVIDENCE FOLDERS FOR tools/hooks/evidence_guard.py
#
# Copy this file to `.claude/evidence-dirs.local` — WITHOUT the .example suffix — and put one
# folder name per line. That file is gitignored and must stay that way.
#
# WHY IT IS SEPARATE FROM THE GUARD. Two evidence folders are named in the guard itself
# because their names are already public in this repository. The TEST-DOCUMENT folder's name
# is not, and naming it here would publish it — the same reasoning that keeps the 93-pattern
# scan list and the corpus-descriptor list outside the repo (CLAUDE.md 5.4): the scanner
# ships, the list never does.
#
# UNTIL YOU CREATE THAT FILE, THE TEST-DOCUMENT FOLDER IS NOT GUARDED. That is a real gap and
# it is stated rather than papered over. `tests/test_evidence_guard.py` says so in its own
# closing output.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored. Matching is case-insensitive and on the
# folder NAME as it appears in a command, so a bare name is enough — no path, no wildcards.
#
# Example (invented, not a real folder):
# my-test-documents
